==Battleground==
*30 [[Croconator]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*4 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 12 seconds<sup>360f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Super Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>.
*5 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 63.33 seconds<sup>1,900f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*6 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage features only [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] and [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies, making the optimal meatshield choice [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]], ideally with a Research [[Cat Combo]]. Bring [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] such as [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] or [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] to deal with the Super Metal Hippoes. M. Ost can be dealt with using [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] or any [[Uncanny Legends]] [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] like [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Dr. Nova]]: Nova can consistently Slow all enemies in this stage and does not need to worry about Curse.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Superstar Koneko]]: Being able to both deal [[Critical Hit]]s and Slow Relics, Koneko is a solid pick for this stage. Just keep in mind that she is very RNG-reliant, therefore, when bringing her to this stage, it's best to err on the side of caution and bring other Critical Hitters.

